# Copy to .env and fill in. The CLI auto-loads the nearest .env (walking up from
# the working directory), or you can export these in your shell instead.
#
# Pick ONE of the two setups below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A) OpenAI (hosted)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Optional model override (default: gpt-4o-mini). Also honored: OPENAI_MODEL.
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B) Fully local via Ollama -- no OpenAI, no API key.
#    Run `ollama serve` and `ollama pull llama3.1`, then set:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1
#
# (Equivalent one-off: `python -m callintel run --ollama --model llama3.1`.)
# Any OpenAI-compatible server works via LLM_BASE_URL / --base-url.
